.TH MIMIR-NODE 1 2026-11-20 "mimir" "Mimir"
.SH NAME
mimir-node \- one node of a Mimir cluster, a Redis-compatible distributed database
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mimir-node
.RI [ option ...]
.br
.B mimir-node
.B \-\-cluster\-state
.I dir
.B \-\-init\-state
.br
.B mimir-node \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mimir-node
serves the Redis protocol (RESP2 and RESP3) on its port and is one node of a
Mimir cluster. A client may connect to any node, and every command works
whichever node it talks to: every write commits by agreement on a majority of
the cluster, with no leader. Without a state directory the node is a
throwaway cluster of one, its cluster port on loopback.
.PP
It reports what it does as one JSON object per line on standard output:
.B listening
(its ports and node id),
.B founded ,
.B caught_up
and
.BR stopped .
.SH SETTINGS
Every setting is a key in a YAML file, a
.B MIMIR_*
environment variable and a flag, read in that order, each overriding the one
before. The file is
.BR \-\-config ,
.BR $MIMIR_CONFIG ,
or
.I /usr/local/etc/mimir/config.yaml
when it exists; then
.I secrets.yaml
beside it. A value that cannot be used is refused at start, naming where it
came from.
.TP
.BR \-\-listen " \fIaddr\fR (listen.host, MIMIR_LISTEN)"
The address to serve clients on; 0.0.0.0 by default.
.TP
.BR \-\-port " \fIn\fR (listen.port, MIMIR_PORT)"
The client port; 6379 by default.
.TP
.BR \-\-tls\-port " \fIn\fR, " \-\-tls\-certificate " \fIpem\fR, " \-\-tls\-key " \fIpem\fR (tls.*)"
A TLS client port, with its certificate chain and key.
.TP
.BR \-\-tls\-client\-ca " \fIpem\fR (tls.client_ca)"
Require client certificates signed by this bundle.
.TP
.BR \-\-databases " \fIn\fR (databases)"
The number of databases SELECT may choose, 1 to 1024; 1 by default.
.TP
.BR \-\-auth\-plaintext " (auth.plaintext)"
Take AUTH and HELLO ... AUTH on a plaintext connection. Without it a password
is accepted only over TLS.
.TP
.BR \-\-user " \fIline\fR (acl.users, a list)"
A line of a Valkey ACL file, such as
.BR "user app on >secret ~app:* +@all" .
Best kept in
.IR secrets.yaml .
.TP
.BR \-\-notify\-keyspace\-events " \fIletters\fR (notify.keyspace_events)"
Valkey's keyspace notification classes.
.TP
.B latency.tracking
Whether each command's run is timed for LATENCY HISTOGRAM, as Valkey's
latency-tracking; on by default. Set it to false in the file, or
.B MIMIR_LATENCY_TRACKING=false
in the environment, to turn it off; CONFIG SET latency-tracking changes it
while the node runs.
.TP
.BR \-\-cluster\-key " \fIfile\fR, " \-\-cluster\-state " \fIdir\fR (cluster.key, cluster.state)"
The cluster's shared key file and this node's state directory.
.TP
.BR \-\-cluster\-listen " \fIaddr\fR, " \-\-cluster\-port " \fIn\fR, " \-\-cluster\-advertise " \fIhost\fR"
Where the node listens for other nodes (0.0.0.0:16379 by default) and the
host they dial.
.TP
.BR \-\-genesis " \fIid\fR (cluster.genesis, a list)"
The founding nodes' ids. Without it, a node with no bootstrap peers founds a
cluster alone.
.TP
.BR \-\-bootstrap " \fIhost:port\fR (cluster.bootstrap, a list)"
Other nodes' cluster ports, to join through.
.TP
.BR \-\-shards " \fIn\fR (cluster.shards)"
The shard count, 1 to 8192, the same on every node; 256 by default.
.TP
.BR \-\-cluster\-name " \fIname\fR, " \-\-cluster\-domain " \fIdomain\fR"
This node's name and failure domain.
.TP
.BR \-\-log\-level " \fIlevel\fR, " \-\-log\-format " text|json"
ALL, DEBUG, INFO, WARN or ERROR; text or JSON lines.
.TP
.BR \-\-seconds " \fIn\fR"
Run for this long, 0 (the default) until SIGTERM or SIGINT.
.TP
.B \-\-init\-state
Make the state directory and this node's id, print
.B {"event":"initialised","id":"..."}
and exit. A cluster of several founders names each founder's id in every
founder's genesis list, so each id is made first. The state votes as new on
its first start only.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/mimir/config.yaml
The packaged settings: a cluster of one on loopback.
.TP
.I /etc/mimir/secrets.yaml
The users, mode 600.
.TP
.I /etc/mimir/cluster.key
The cluster key, made by the package; every node of a cluster has the same one.
.TP
.I /var/lib/mimir
The node's state directory.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR redis-cli (1),
.B https://github.com/tomdionysus/mimir
